    "extract": "Jayaco River is a 14.58 km (9.06 mi) long river in the Dominican Republic province of Monseñor Nouel. A part of the Yuna River watershed, the river originates in Hoyo Redonda within the Cordillera Central mountain range.\nThe river flows east from its source and reaches its mouth at the Rincón Reservoir, a part of the Jima River.",
    "extract_html": "<p><b>Jayaco River</b> is a 14.58 km (9.06 mi) long river in the Dominican Republic province of Monseñor Nouel. A part of the Yuna River watershed, the river originates in Hoyo Redonda within the Cordillera Central mountain range.\nThe river flows east from its source and reaches its mouth at the Rincón Reservoir, a part of the Jima River.</p>"
